//! Randomized fuzz / stress harness for the pty-output path.
//!
//! Feeds generated byte streams through the ANSI [`Processor`] into a
//! [`TerminalModel`] (and so through `BlockList` -> `Block` -> `GridHandler`),
//! interleaved with model operations (resize/reflow, lifecycle hooks, `clear`,
//! find), and reports panics, pathologically slow inputs, hangs and invariant
//! violations.
//!
//! Both tests are `#[ignore]`d so they never run in normal CI. Run with:
//!
//! ```text
//! cargo nextest run -p warp --lib --features gui --run-ignored only -E 'test(/terminal_fuzz/)'
//! ```
//!
//! Environment:
//!
//! | variable | default | meaning |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_SEED` | time-based (printed) | master seed |
//! | `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_ITERS` | 2000 | number of cases; 0 = unlimited (bounded by `SECS`) |
//! | `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_SECS` | 60 | wall-clock budget; stops early when reached |
//! | `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_MAX_LEN` | 65536 | max stream bytes per case |
//! | `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_CASE` | unset | run only this case index of `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_SEED` |
//! | `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_OUT` | `$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/fuzz-cases` or `<workspace>/target/fuzz-cases` | where failing cases are dumped |
//! | `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_SLOW_MS` | 2000 | a case slower than this is a "slow input" failure |
//! | `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_HANG_SECS` | 60 | a case still running after this is a hang; the run stops |
//! | `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_HUGE_IMAGES` | 0 | 1 = allow huge kitty/iTerm image dimensions (may allocate GBs) |
//! | `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_IN_FLIGHT` | 1 | 0 = do not write the in-flight case before running it |
//! | `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_BACKTRACE` | 0 | 1 = capture a backtrace for every panic |
//! | `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_REPLAY` | unset | `terminal_fuzz_replay`: path to a dumped `.ops` or `.bin` |
//!
//! Every case is generated from its own RNG seeded by `(seed, case index)`, so a
//! single case is reproducible with `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_SEED=<seed> PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_CASE=<index>`.
//! Each failing case is also dumped as `<seed>-<case>.bin` (the concatenated pty
//! bytes) plus `<seed>-<case>.ops` (the op list, which refers into the `.bin`), and
//! `terminal_fuzz_replay` replays it from `PHOSPHOR_FUZZ_REPLAY=<path>`. Before
//! each case runs it is written to `in-flight-<seed>.{bin,ops}`, so a case that
//! aborts the process (stack overflow, OOM, double panic) can still be replayed.
//!
//! Each case runs on its own thread so that a hang can be detected; the thread
//! cannot be killed, so a hang ends the run after the case is dumped.

